			<div class="head">
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4828196">
																	<a href="/forum/t-13867910/draft-disconnected-restroom#post-4828196">Re: Draft &quot;Disconnected Restroom&quot;</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/oystershell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2796394); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2796394&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606356497" alt="Oystershell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2796394)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/oystershell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2796394); return false;" >Oystershell</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606353966 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2020 01:26</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50864/help:drafts-critique">Writing Help / Help: Drafts Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13867910/draft-disconnected-restroom">Draft &quot;Disconnected Restroom&quot;</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828196">
									

<p>Note, I am not the most well-read or experienced user. Reach out to members of the Butterfly Roster for more informed criticism.</p>
<p>Phrases in quotes are my suggestions.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Line&nbsp;By&nbsp;Line</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hiya&nbsp;howdy&nbsp;howya&nbsp;doin</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The hallway leading to SCP-XXXX has to be guarded by at least one security personnel at all times.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The hallway <em>is</em> to be guarded. Passive voice. Also, the &quot;at least one&quot; clause is unnecessary. How can a hallway be guarded by less than one guard?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Cleaning staff may flush if they hear noises coming from SCP-XXXX, but must record when they do so.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Cleaning staff are to flush if they hear noises coming from SCP-XXXX, and must make record of doing so.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>At no time should SCP-XXXX be used as originally intended.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Too vague. If we haven't read the article yet, we don't know what the original intent is.<br />
&quot;At no time should SCP-XXXX be used as a waste receptacle.&quot;</p>
<p>Side note: add line breaks between paragraphs. Necessary for readability.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The building housing SCP-XXXX has been bought by the Foundation and is used as [REDACTED]. To the outside it is advertised as telemarketing firm. Unauthorized entry should be responded to by calling the local police.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The ConProcs don't generally need detail about the Site cover stories unless it's related to the nature of the anomaly. Also, there are armed guards in this building. Involvement of local police is redundant. &quot;Provisional Site-XXXX has been established in the building housing SCP-XXXX. Unauthorized entry is forbidden.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It consists of two adjacent restrooms, one for males and one for females.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;It consists of two adjacent restrooms with standard male/female designations.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Both areas have two sinks and four stalls</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Both areas possess&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The restrooms are working as normally expected.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;SCP-XXXX functions as expected for a public restroom.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>as underground exploration and sub-surface scans showed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;have shown&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Electricity however is connected as expected.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Commas after &quot;electricity&quot; and &quot;however&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The planning company found that no plans existed where the water supply or sewer access was depicted for the building housing SCP-XXXX.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Contractors found that water supply and sewer access were absent from all plans of the building.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A check of the canalization confirmed that no access to the building exists and the Foundation was informed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;A check of the canalization confirmed the absence of water mains and sewer lines. The Foundation was subsequently notified.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The initially deployed MTF ███ secured SCP-XXXX under cover of the reconstruction project which was immediately canceled.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No reason to censor an MTF. &quot;MTF-BLANK initially secured SCP-XXXX under cover of the renovation project. All construction plans were subsequently cancelled.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The employees of the offices in the building were detained and questioned. During the interviews medical and psychological examinations were conducted as well.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Employees of the offices in the building were detained, questioned, and subjected to medical and psychological examination.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There was no indication of any influence on the persons working in the building.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is simply untrue, given the information you provide in the next sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Vitruv noted during the interviews that many employees had rather fond memories of the restrooms, finding relief being there, using the facilities or simply running the water.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Dr. Vitruv noted that during the interviews, many employees recalled fond memories of the restrooms. Subjects reported feelings of calm or relief when using the facilities or simply running the water.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Sampling the tap water, it was discovered that it matches the composition and requirements of most of the tap water in the United States as shown in document XXXX-2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Sampling of the tap water revealed that it meets all composition requirements in the state of ██. It possesses no components that might aid in tracing its origin. For details on the composition of water obtained from SCP-XXXX, see Document-XXXX-2.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For the used water / waste see Post-Experiment report XXXX-4</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;For compositional analysis of black- and grey-water obtained from SCP-XXXX, see Post-experiment Report XXXX-4.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Experiment XXXX-1: Audio Transcript</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Add a note clarifying that the exploration is taking place via drone.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Frank:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Use Frank's full blacked-out name.</p>
<p>Note: Line breaks should be added throughout this log.</p>
<p>Note2: During this log there are multiple instances of ellipses (&quot;&#8230;&quot;) that are spaced incorrectly. They should be placed directly after the word they follow with no space in-between.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>As per experiment report XXXX-4-B and under strict safety measures four point one litres of [REDACTED] were inserted into the sewer section of SCP-XXXX using the first booth of the men's room. The liquid was flushed using a total of eighty litres of SCP-XXXX tap water. As [REDACTED] is a potent and safe tracer it was believed to enable us to identify the exit of SCP-XXXX. Unfortunately we did not manage to confirm any result.<br />
About two months after the experiment a meteorological satellite under control of the ████ found traces of the used substance in the southern Atlantic. It is currently unknown if this finding correlates to SCP-XXXX.<br />
I am awaiting clearance to repeat the experiment.<br />
Dr. Vitruv</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I have multiple issues with this note. Firstly, redacting the tracer liquid adds nothing to the article and makes the note significantly harder to read. Appears as if you simply did not want to research a traceable liquid. Similarly, there is no reason to redact the controller of the satellite. Lastly, there are multiple instances of missing commas. Dr. Vitruv should sign the note with a dash, like this:<br />
&quot;&#8212;Dr. Vitruv&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a man calling himself Michael (actual identity unknown, assumed to be a local homeless man)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;a local homeless man calling himself &quot;Michael&quot; (actual identity unconfirmed)&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The hallway guard was absent at that time due to a medical emergency.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems like gross incompetence on behalf of whoever is managing containment. Perhaps,</p>
<p>&quot;The hallway guard was momentarily absent during shift turnover.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>According to post-incident interrogation Michael had to urgently use the restroom, so he opened the (due to the emergency unlocked) front door and walked into SCP-XXXX.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;According to post-incident interrogation Michael urgently needed to use the restroom, and therefore entered SCP-XXXX through the main door, which was momentarily unlocked due to REASON&quot;</p>
<p>Note: you're going to have to come up with a new reason for the door being unlocked. I can't think of one off the top of my head.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He described hearing a violent grown directly after he flushed - and experiencing a sharp pain in the lower abdomen before loosing consciousness.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;He described hearing a violent <em>groan</em> directly after flushing, and experienced a sharp lower-abdominal pain before <em>losing</em> consciousness.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>bleeding from a head wound due to a broken door.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The meaning of this is unclear. How exactly did Michael hurt his head?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Overall&nbsp;thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">phew&nbsp;that&nbsp;took&nbsp;a&nbsp;while</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>While I overall enjoyed this skip, I don't believe it's quite ready for the mainlist in its current state. Specifically, the anomalous effect needs to be fleshed out. It's just&#8230; missing a little <em>something.</em></p>
<p>Now, I very much enjoy how your article creates mystery, so going forward you have a tightrope to walk between showing us interesting and intriguing effects, and maintaining the simplicity of the premise. That's a difficult task, but I believe it can be done.</p>
<p>In conclusion I would say that perhaps 10% more information about the anomaly would add some much-needed intrigue, but 15% would be too much. Act on that as you see fit.</p>
<p>I wish you the best of luck and hope to see this on the mainlist sometime soon.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Have a great day!</p>

