			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828188">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The anomaly was a former channel on the media site “YouTube” that was active from 11/15/19 to 11/15/20 exactly one year from its creation.</p>
<p>The channel uploaded what would seem like fun original content but was littered with cognitohazardous material that has now been completely neutralized. Two humanoids are present in every video and host the channel. Both entities are almost identical to two other famous people but are not the same people.</p>
<p>Subjects who view any of the 365 videos are instantly met with a clock that counts down starting from 365:00:00. The anomaly’s effects immediate initiate at the start of every video by infecting and manipulating the subject’s mind making them perceive the two entities as gods and begin to worship the two entities in nonsensical and sometimes violent ways. Afflicted subjects attempt to spread the anomaly through social media and other chat related applications.</p>
<p>The anomaly can not be deleted directly by YouTube since attempts to do so crash all electronic devices.</p>
<p>The two entities seen in every video seem to not be a part of our dimension but from another reality. Since they cannot be located and have been seen with anomalous items that do cannot exist in our reality.<br />
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The Narrative would dictate all of the foundations attempts to neutralize the anomaly and work with YouTube to contain the anomaly from spreading. Millions of viewers have already been infected by the anomaly and spread of the anomaly drastically increases. The Foundation worries that an AK end of the world scenario could occur as tens of millions of people rapidly fall under the anomaly’s influence. As governments collapse and people perform violent rituals in the streets the channel finally reaches its climatic end</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Based on a real experiment conducted on the same website.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The central narrative would begin by detailing the small amount of infection but slowly starts getting worse and worse until the end. Not all details described here it would be too long.</p>

