						<a href="/forum/t-13877616/medicine-man-first-scp-idea">Medicine Man - first scp idea</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828181">
									

<p><strong>It just feels boring, basic, and not a good fit for the site.</strong></p>
<p>The Bold Statement says my first thought of this SCP, and without further statements, here's the review.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">The&nbsp;Review</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>The Pitch</strong><br />
It just feels boring, and outdated. It did not peak my interest what so ever. It didn't make me think, <em>Huh, that's a neat SCP Idea</em>, I just read it and grew more bored of the concept with every sentence. A sculpture is an something that has been used many times of the Wiki, as doing a simple tag search I found 55 SCPs that revolve around a Sculpture as an SCP, So already, that's a problem, you could find another object, any other object, and I would be fine. And for it to revolve around you dropping your guard just feels very &quot;SCP-173&quot; like, it's too similar.<br />
Now the way the Sculpture has its anomalous effect is that you lose attention in the Sculpture, that just sounds very basic, and boring. Now, to where the Medicine Man switches to another sculpture, why not just contain him when he's switching? Don't add shit where he's &quot;Impossible to contain.&quot; Cause then that's going to make this entire SCP just feel like a child's piece of literature. Also how the fuck would the SCP Foundation know if a Sculpture has a consciousness? As you make it seem like you make a person an object that can't move, speak, breathe, touch, blink, etc. Well how would anyone know that the Sculpture was conscious?</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong><br />
Oh boy, this is what pissed me off the most out of your Idea, the fact that you think the Foundation would Attempt to recruit a semi-dangerous SCP who tells people they have lost the ability to concentrate, and could switch a person to an eternal hell of not moving, is a damn ludicrous thought! They would secure this SCP down in a single room, maybe test it a bit, and they would probably never use it again. The SCP site is a prison, not a place of recruitment or a hotel, but a place of exploitation, research, and containment. If an SCP shows any sign of being dangerous, I would think it's safe to assume that they would never want to use it for the good, as any SCP could have undiscovered traits that could cause major harm to the world.</p>
<p><strong>Conclusion</strong><br />
I may have been harsh, and this may be your first SCP Idea, but it just doesn't seem to fit for a modern like SCP, maybe a few years ago the site would let this fly but times have changed.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

